If your AC after the Mines and Sokoban is only -5, then I am guessing
you have not bought protection from the Minetown priest.

Playing Tourists exclusively, I rely on my pet to get me to the temple.
 There are various ways to get a lot of cash, and if I arrive in the
temple intact I should have about 3000 zorkmids and, ideally, still be
only level 1.  When I walk out of that temple again I will have a naked
AC of 0 or 1, and still with the help of the pet I will gather and sort
every piece of armor I can.  Carrying capacity is a problem with such a
low level character, but this only means it takes a little longer.
Before trying Sokoban I will be AC -10 or better.  Before going to
Mines End I will have thoroughly cleaned the mines - again, time
consuming, but I am gaining experience in the process, and usually
improving my weaponry and gathering other useful items of kit.

Boredom is usually my greatest enemy.  The very early game is a flurry
of activity, the journey through the mines is predictable but still
interesting, and then there is an interlude of the game where it is
essential to tidy up and prepare yourself before diving below Sokoban.
Take more care in that preparation, and you'll probably extend your
performance.



